---
source: crates/dreamd-cli/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: "subcommand_help(\"service\")"
---
Manage the per-user service that runs `dreamd watch` (Linux systemd --user unit / macOS LaunchAgent)

Usage: service <COMMAND>

Commands:
  install  Write a user-scope service for `dreamd watch` and enable it now (Linux systemd --user / macOS LaunchAgent)
  start    Start the user-scope service (systemctl --user start / launchctl kickstart)
  restart  Bounce the user-scope service (systemctl --user restart / launchctl kickstart -k)
  status   Report whether the user-scope service is running (systemd / launchd). Daemon-level liveness (UDS) is `dreamd status`
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help
